# The Omarchy desktop surface, trimmed to what Arch Linux ARM plausibly builds
# for armv7h. Everything here is best effort: the machine still boots and logs
# in without any of it, and whatever pacman cannot resolve is named in
# /var/lib/omarchy/armv7-packages.report to be built from source.
#
# Deliberately absent, because they come from the Omarchy repo
# (pkgs.omarchy.org), which publishes x86_64 only: aether, cliamp, herdr,
# omacalc, omacut, omarchy-nvim, omawrite, tensaku, tobi-try, ttfx. Also absent:
# the x86-only ones (dotnet-runtime, moonlight-qt, gpu-screen-recorder) and the
# heavy builds no RK3288 should attempt (libreoffice-fresh, kdenlive,
# obs-studio). See docs/armv7.md.

hyprland
# guiutils, not qtutils: hyprland-qtutils is deprecated upstream and the Arch
# package that replaced it is hyprland-guiutils, which is what
# install/omarchy-base.packages asks for on x86_64 too.
hyprland-guiutils
hyprpicker
hyprsunset
uwsm
quickshell
qt6-wayland
qt6-declarative
qt6-imageformats
xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland
xdg-terminal-exec
sddm

# Firefox stands in for Chromium, which Arch Linux ARM builds for aarch64 but
# not armv7h. Omarchy's browser plumbing handles a Firefox default; its web app
# launchers open a window instead of a Chromium --app frame.
firefox

foot
nautilus
imv

# Tools Omarchy's own commands shell out to: gum for the menu prompts,
# imagemagick for theme and background handling, pamixer for the audio
# controls, qrencode for the QR capture, yt-dlp for the video handoff.
gum
imagemagick
pamixer
qrencode
yt-dlp
inotify-tools
socat
fontconfig
lazygit

# Adwaita in place of yaru-icon-theme, which armv7h does not carry: without an
# icon theme, GTK applications draw missing-image placeholders.
adwaita-icon-theme
mpv
mpv-mpris

gnome-keyring
libsecret
gnome-themes-extra
yaru-icon-theme
noto-fonts
noto-fonts-emoji
ttf-jetbrains-mono-nerd

grim
slurp
wl-clipboard
wtype
udiskie

bat
btop
eza
fastfetch
fd
fzf
jq
plocate
ripgrep
starship
tmux
zoxide

power-profiles-daemon
ufw
